      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page (titled \u0022Guarded Write Journal\u0022) describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**.\n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n- Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or a note that it didn\u0027t exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal.\n- If an agent run fails (due to a turn cap being exceeded, an unrecoverable error, or all attempted writes being denied), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed and deleting newly created files.\n- This provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself serves as the transaction log and is held only in the process\u0027s memory during a single run.\n- The Query agent doesn\u0027t use the rollback path since it has no write capability, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 2520,
      "output_tokens": 221
